// data/mindat-species-refs.json5 — THE CITATIONS REGISTRY for the per-mine mindat
// valid-species sweep (boss capture project, begun 2026-07-25).
//
// WHAT THIS IS: the machine-readable central record of every mindat Mineral List the
// boss captures for a scenario. The prose verdicts (what each list votes on vs the
// sim's seed-42 output) live in the scenario's own `notes` array in scenarios.json5 —
// this file is the SOURCE-OF-RECORD side: locality identity, capture provenance, and
// the species list itself as data, so a future tools/mindat-census.mjs can run the
// fleet-wide cross-check (sim output vs record) automatically instead of by hand.
//
// CITATION FORMAT, per entry:
//   scenario        — the scenarios.json5 key this list licenses
//   locality        — the mindat page title as captured (the boss's chosen grain)
//   mindat_id       — mindat Locality ID when visible in the capture; null = not
//                     captured (record it on the next visit — the ID is the stable
//                     citation; page titles drift)
//   url             — canonical form https://www.mindat.org/loc-<id>.html when the
//                     id is known; null otherwise (NEVER guess an id)
//   captured        — date of the boss's screenshot capture
//   source          — how the data arrived (all boss-supplied screenshots so far;
//                     screenshot-limited entries may CROP — a species missing here
//                     is a lead, not a verdict, until checked on the live page)
//   valid_count     — the page's own "N valid minerals" footer
//   tl_count        — type localities among them, when the page states it
//   species         — the VALID list (species level; varieties in parentheses in the
//                     scenario notes are collapsed to their species here)
//   varieties_of_note, erroneous (struck-through), questioned (italic-?) — recorded
//                     separately; ERRONEOUS AND QUESTIONED ENTRIES NEVER LICENSE.
//   notes_ref       — where the sim-verdict prose lives
//
// METHODOLOGY (boss): pick the ICONIC SUB-LOCALITY so the data is consistent — and
// the sub-locality must be the ORE BODY, NOT THE TOWNSITE (the Warren/Bisbee page:
// 6 species, no copper — recording it would have voted to kill the whole scenario).
// SPATIAL GRAIN: a flag means "not at THIS locality"; the boss adjudicates
// mine-grain vs district-grain (horizontal) and cave-stage vs ore-body (vertical)
// before anything dies.

